;; :remove-multiple-non-indenting-spaces? makes rule :align-forms (see ../harness-seed/resources/agent-rules.edn) true rather
;; than aspirational. Without it cljfmt accepts `:else     x` silently, and the
;; rule told agents it would fail the gate — a rule that misdescribes its gate
;; erodes every other rule (§09: gates and rules are one system, not two).
{:sort-ns-references? true
 :remove-multiple-non-indenting-spaces? true}
